# Dump the original game's sprite state, to diff against the reconstruction's.
#
# Two steps, because the breakpoint address cannot be written as an expression here. The original is
# stripped, so _mh_execute_header has no symbol to resolve, and this attach cannot install the
# expression checkers in any case -- which is why `br set -a <expr>` fails outright.
#
# Step one: source this file. It prints the image's load address and nothing else.
#
#   (lldb) command source /var/jb/var/mobile/rb458-orig-sprites.lldb
#
# Read the address of the "REFLEC BEAT plus" module from the output -- the [0x...] on its line -- and
# add 0x31090, which is EmitMatrixSprites. If the module loads at 0x104b18000, that is 0x104b49090.
#
# Step two: paste these four lines, substituting that sum for ADDR:
#
#   breakpoint set -a ADDR
#   breakpoint command add -o "memory read -f d -s 4 -c 2 `$x0 + 0x120`" -o "memory read -f f -s 4 -c 8 `*(uint64_t *)($x0 + 0xd8)`" -o "memory read -f f -s 4 -c 8 `*(uint64_t *)($x0 + 0xe8)`" -o "memory read -f f -s 4 -c 8 `*(uint64_t *)($x0 + 0xe0)`" -o "memory read -f f -s 4 -c 8 `*(uint64_t *)($x0 + 0xf0)`" -o "memory read -f f -s 4 -c 8 `*(uint64_t *)($x0 + 0xf8)`" 1
#   breakpoint modify --auto-continue true 1
#   continue
#
# Register arithmetic in backticks needs no symbols, so it should evaluate where the
# _mh_execute_header form did not. If even `$x0 + 0x120` fails, say so: the fallback is to stop at
# the breakpoint, `register read x0`, and read the offsets from that literal by hand.
#
# The reads are, in order: capacity and count; then for sprites 0 to 3, the position pairs, the
# anchor pairs, the size pairs, the UV origin pairs and the UV size pairs. They line up field for
# field with the reconstruction's own snapshot lines.
#
# The member offsets are the binary's own, from its destructor at 0x30c80, which frees the nine
# sprite arrays between 0xd8 and 0x118, and from SetSpritePosition at 0x5a0c4, which bounds the
# index against the capacity at 0x120 and reads the position array from 0xd8:
#
#     +0x0d8 position   +0x0e0 size      +0x0e8 anchor    +0x0f0 uv origin   +0x0f8 uv size
#     +0x100 rotation   +0x108 scale x   +0x110 scale y   +0x118 colour
#     +0x120 capacity   +0x124 count     +0x130 index vbo +0x134 array vbo   +0x138 texture
#
# Every batch taking the matrix path hits this once per frame, so expect volume. Let it run a
# second, interrupt, and read back. The gauge batch is the one reporting a count of sixteen.

image list -h -o -f "REFLEC BEAT plus"
